{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1495018-a-question-about-mummies-and-well-other-mummies","id":1495018,"title":"a question about mummies and, well, other mummies.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-15T10:21:27-07:00","id":1495018,"title":"a question about mummies and, well, other mummies.","content":"so i recently found a copy of 'mummy: the resurrection' for a low enough price that i bought it, immediately, and while i wait for it to arrive it's got me thinking of the two previous 'mummy' books and i'm wondering- given the scope of 'mummy: the resurrection,' is there room in that world for the previous mummy variants or does it simply negate them, altogether?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T11:14:41-07:00","id":1495022,"title":"","content":"MTR's answer is yes - there're still some mummies around who used the original Spell of Life, or an analogue, though not many. In MTR terms, they have the flaw Lesser Resurrection, requiring them to roll Stamina when they reach Incapacitated to avoid dying.<br /> <br /> In a broader sense, some mummies who remained faithful to Horus went through the improved Spell of Life via ritual suicide, forming a group known as the Imkhu.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T12:32:16-07:00","id":1495031,"title":"","content":"thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T10:14:37-07:00","id":1495169,"title":"","content":"Mummy 1st ed was so so, but I'm a huge fan of the Mummies presented in the second edition book. They have a lot of potential for different games, even after the changes brought on by Resurrection!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T00:30:10-07:00","id":1495868,"title":"","content":"So I pitched an alternative model for mummies on these boards a while back that attempted to fit the two mummy games together (classic and MTR). People seemed to dig it, and I should probably write it up for STV at some point.<br /> <br /> Initial ideas start here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395618-why-is-mummy-the-resurrection-so-unliked?p=1481073#post1481073\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...73#post1481073</a><br /> <br /> I started fleshing it out here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395618-why-is-mummy-the-resurrection-so-unliked?p=1481176#post1481176\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...76#post1481176</a><br /> <br /> And I rounded it out here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395618-why-is-mummy-the-resurrection-so-unliked?p=1481670#post1481670\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...70#post1481670</a><br /> <br /> The whole thread was full of great ideas.<br /> <br /> One of the ideas I had was that the Shemsu-Heru were the true mummies of old, complete with god-like powers, but you would only focus on these characters for part of the chronicle. The rest of the time you'd play their magical mortal servants, the Amenti.<br /> <br /> Fluff-wise, the changes to magic over the years meant the Shemsu-Heru were harder to awaken with each new age, and required being roused by a ritual by their cult, instead of entirely by their own means.<br /> <br /> The mummies wake up weakened and without some or all of their memories, and they piece everything together over time as they solve mysteries and prepare for the task they were sent here to complete.<br /> <br /> They had long ago bound all the different parts of their souls into the cycle of reincarnation, sort of like the fae or Charon in Ends of Empire. This results in the Amenti: humans who are born carrying the different aspects of the Shemsu-Heru's souls, along with parts of their memories, and who are therefore blessed with a fragment of the power of the mummies. <br /> <br /> These blessed mortals would be the cult leaders who are drawn by flashes of insight and memory to track down ancient Egyptian artefacts and occult secrets from birth. Their quest structure would be to gather together the pieces of their master, interpret the signs of Ma'at and finally resurrect these ancient gods to fulfil the tasks they were being sent back to perform.<br /> <br /> The Amenti would be the distant descendants of loved ones, faithful servants and worshippers of the mummies through the ages, so they would fulfil the role of ghouls or sorcerer consors in the setting. This also fits with the mummy genre's whole &quot;love through the ages&quot; trope.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;bound to reincarnation&quot; thing means you could potentially set each story in completely different time periods (and non-linearly, if you wish to mix it up) with different Amenti, or at different stages of the Amenti's lives (childhood, adolescence, adulthood, middle age, old age...). <br /> <br /> The actions of the Shemsu-Heru and the Amenti in one resurrection cycle would always influence what happens in the next, however, so that there are stakes and consequences.<br /> <br /> You'd be able to play the game troupe style, with one or more Shemsu-Heru primary characters, and then a circle of Amenti tied to each Shemsu-Heru as secondary characters (your Retainers, in VTM terms), with mundane mortals forming the rest of your cult (these would be the equivalent of VTM's Herd or Cult Backgrounds).<br /> <br /> This would give you flexibility, because as one mummy dies again, that player can take on the role of a trusted Amenti. That helps with the OG Mummy problem of Shemsu-Heru dying at different times. <br /> <br /> But there are also real consequences, because when all the mummies die, the cycle turns, and you pick up the pieces months, years or even decades down the line.<br /> <br /> The better you do in each cycle, the shorter the time between resurrections. The worse you do, the longer those resurrections take and the worse the after-effects may be when you wake up.<br /> <br /> You can also change the setting to the Underworld for one off sessions or storylines between the main action in the mortal world, or you can play Amenti games for a change of pace.<br /> <br /> E.g., when the Shemsu-Heru are in the Underworld, you can play the Amenti as they seek out the other missing parts of their master's soul (as these would reincarnate, you wouldn't immediately know where each soul fragment was) and try to track down clues or try to interpret dreams and prophecies to see why your master will be call to the world again -- maybe there's a Bane Mummy on the loose or a cog in the machinery of balance has fallen out of place.<br /> <br /> Then, at the end of this quest, the Amenti would gather, the rite would be performed, and the Shemsu-Heru would rise again. At which point, the Shemsu-Heru return and attempt to fulfil their greater tasks on earth.<br /> <br /> You could, in theory, have imperfect resurrections, where only some of the mummy's soul pieces are brought together, which results in a mummy missing some of its knowledge and powers. This is where Virtues like Memory come back in. They might cap your powers, for example.<br /> <br /> You could also choose which bits your troupe wants to play at which point. You might each have one Shemsu-Heru character and a cult led by the Amenti, or you might have one Shemsu-Heru character you all share and take turns playing, with each of you having a focal Amenti character instead. Whoever fulfils their own part of the quest in the most interesting way gets to play the Shemsu-Heru, or you alternate, or you vote, etc.<br /> <br /> You could play around with which soul fragments each player is responsible for, so when a Shemsu-Heru rises without one or more of those soul fragments, the player (or one of them) who didn't get their Amenti in place in time becomes the ST. <br /> <br /> You can play the Shemsu-Heru in the afterlife, attempting to fulfil a spiritual quest, the outcome of which determines how much information you have and how prepared your cult is when you return to the world (so an incomplete quest might result in missing Amenti or incomplete information, whereas an exceptional quest might give you some bonuses when you resurrect). <br /> <br /> This would then be flipped if you play the Amenti: so your success on the quest in the mortal world determines how your Shemsu-Heru rises, and how complete that resurrection is (any missing parts would be called Hamartia , of course!).<br /> <br /> With some creativity and flexibility in behalf of STs and players, it could be really fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-30-2022, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T14:03:17-07:00","id":1496219,"title":"","content":"oh, i will have to spend some time with this, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T23:36:16-07:00","id":1496241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1495018-a-question-about-mummies-and-well-other-mummies?p=1496219#post1496219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, i will have to spend some time with this, thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Let me know how you get on with it, and what did/didn't work with the core idea/presentation. I can use that to help me refine the ideas a little.<br /> <br /> I haven't started on the mechanics yet, as that's the next big beast to conquer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T18:31:31-08:00","id":1496765,"title":"","content":"I played a<i> Mummy</i>, I think it was 2e, that had memory for a virtue, in a VtM. It was a fun game; I was really powerful and ancient, but didn't know my full potential. Seriously though, my character had Weather Control of five: I could literally end a civilization if I wanted to. <br /> <br /> I used the <i>Mummy</i> book as a basis for a WoD game set in ancient-Egypt using the Sorcerer book. It worked. <br /> <br /> I've never read MtR, so, like most White-Wolf games, yes, you may have to convert them. <br /> <br /> I also enjoyed the Purified from the NWoD <i>Immortals</i> book. They seemed weaker and more limited, but they made more sense. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}